  6. WHY THIS REPORT IS LOAD BEARING: THE SHARED SEAM IDIOM
  ==========================================================================

  This module's single test class is one of the six mocking framework rewrites, and it is the
  SECOND SITE of the migration's construction mock seam idiom. The sibling AWS tool module's
  transcribe test class is that idiom's reference implementation, and this module deliberately
  shares the one pattern rather than inventing a second.

  At the base commit this class carried exactly ONE call site that the rewrite must change: a
  single constructor interception of a JDK file stream type, at line 128 of the test source.
  That statement is byte for byte identical to the three interceptions in the sibling module,
  which is the verified proof that the idiom is genuinely shared rather than merely similar.

  Construction mocking CANNOT intercept a type loaded by the bootstrap class loader, so that
  interception could not be converted mechanically. The rewrite instead introduces a narrow,
  test visible stream supplier seam, which is the minimum change that preserves the assertions.
  Note pointedly that the bootstrap class loader constraint was answered with a SEAM, not by
  widening module access: see section 7.

  Three obligations follow, and they are what make this folder consequential:

    1. EVERY ASSERTION IS LEFT UNMODIFIED BY THE REWRITE. Only the mocking mechanism changes.
       The eight testcase names enumerated below are the acceptance criterion for that claim:
       they must survive the rewrite exactly. This archive is the before picture for a rewrite
       whose whole point is that behaviour does not move, and it is emphatically NOT licence to
       exclude the class.
    2. CAPTURE HAD TO PRECEDE THE REWRITE, NOT FOLLOW IT. Once rewritten, the original mechanism
       is gone and no later action can reconstruct this evidence. The working tree on this branch
       already carries the rewritten class, with zero occurrences of the retired framework, so
       the enumeration below was read from the PRE REWRITE class at the base commit.
    3. A REVIEWER COMPARING THE TWO AWS TOOL FOLDERS SHOULD FIND THE IDIOM IDENTICAL. The
       sibling module's own archive anticipated this folder before it was declared; this
       statement is its reciprocal.

  Also verified from that source and reflected in the enumeration below: the module declares
